			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://indieweb.social/@nachtfunke\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>nachtfunke</span></a></span> I'm not particularly plugged into the JS discourse, but my recollection is early on they were really pulling the reins on it, saying this really exists for these specific use cases. But they naturally wanted to monetize and that means holding the attention of a certain kind of personality.</p><p>The irony - to me - is that I learned *so much* about CSS from watching Adam's early \"build with Tailwind\" streams.</p>",
