				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/291/886/080/250/362/original/533c7d9904760762.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2023-03-22T17:54:06.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> the more I think about it, the more I see CSS‘ unique quality, which makes it unparalleled to work with, is what is at the same time the reason for why it is considered almost incompatible with industrial grade programming, expressed by JavaScripts role on the web.</p><p>CSS is made for humans, authors. Everyday people can work with it. I’ve taught absolute beginners CSS and HTML. They immediately got it. CSS is too human centered for Industry.</p>",
