		{
			"id": "110069551577533301",
			"parentId": "110068471736194876",
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@fedbysandrine/110069551543983751",
			"author": {
				"name": "Sandrine",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@fedbysandrine",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/301/154/117/521/544/original/df9008be46f71c44.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-03-22T23:34:29.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@ardouglass\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>ardouglass</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Yes and the consequence that a11y assessments are becoming HTML 101.</p><p>After input nested in a dozen of div with JS-injected classes to handle focus and hover states, this week I have main nav links being divs with click event, a skip anchor link with no destination.</p><p>Question: can you call yourself a web developer if you don't even know how to make links as links are the absolute foundation of the web existence ? 🤷‍♀️</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
